## Current Mock AI Behavior

The Edge Function is not using a paid AI provider yet. It is deterministic mock logic, so it does not create model-token charges. Copilot usage in VS Code is separate from Marginalia's Supabase and Edge Function costs.

The mock extractor recognizes a small set of explicit character, location, and item details, including scar evidence such as:

```text
Mira touched the scar above her left eye.
```

It returns a structured suggestion similar to:

```json
{
  "type": "character_update",
  "entityId": "remote-entity-id",
  "field": "physical",
  "operation": "append",
  "value": "Mira has a scar above her left eye.",
  "evidence": "Mira touched the scar above her left eye.",
  "sourceLine": 1,
  "status": "pending"
}
```

The current source line is calculated from preserved rich-text line breaks. The frontend stores approved provenance in the character entity's JSON data under `provenance`.

